item.description:
In a candid conversation, US Sen. Raphael Warnock (D-GA) explains why voters haven’t necessarily fallen in love with the Democratic brand, why the party must center people over politics, and how the path to power runs through the South.&nbsp;

This show was edited by Kasia Broussalian, fact checked by Sarah Schweppe, mixed by Shannon Mahoney, video edited by Christopher Snyder, and hosted by Astead Herndon.

Photo caption: US Sen. Raphael Warnock (D-GA) reacts while taking the stage to speak during the What's Next summit at Mission Ballroom on November 13, 2026 in Denver, Colorado. Photo by Mark Makela/Getty Images.

You can also watch this episode on youtube.com/vox. Listen to Today, Explained ad-free by becoming a Vox Member: vox.com/members. New Vox members get $20 off their membership right now.&nbsp;


